### SYNTHETIC. THIS IS NOT A METAL GREEN REFERENCE AND MUST NEVER BE CITED AS ONE.
### It is a hand-built capture whose only job is to prove that jetson-sync1.spec CAN
### go green -- that its 17 REQUIREs and its end-of-run marker are simultaneously
### satisfiable, and that a clean boot trips none of its 18 FORBIDs. A scorer that
### has only ever been run against captures that red has not been tested; this file
### is the other direction.
###
### PROVENANCE, line by line: every witness below is the VERBATIM wire text of the
### first line that satisfied that rule in the boot5b/desk sitting
### (~/unaos-bench/capture/line-acm0/orin.log), EXCEPT the JD2/JD4 takeover pair,
### which is rewritten to the CURRENT post-fold shape from main.rs:2890/2898 -- the
### `path=jd2-console-pump; ` discriminator that the two stale-image FORBIDs at
### jetson-sync1.spec:1490/1491 exist to demand. That rewrite is the whole point:
### the old capture reds on those two rows precisely because it predates the fold.
###
### The tail block is a BOOT A (conwin1) shape -- orinconwin / orinfurn / orinstkdepth
### / orinrast -- so the PENDING rows those instruments own are shown promoting. A
### BOOT B (supstate1) capture will not carry them, and that asymmetry is legitimate;
### see the COVERAGE section of scripts/orin-specscore.py for which rules each image
### can and cannot fire.
